Your project uses **MSTest v3 (3.8.0)** on net8.0. Here are the breaking changes that apply to your code, plus key ones to know about:

### Directly affects your code

**`[ExpectedException]` removed** (lines 9, 16) — Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()` inside the test body:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

Same pattern for `Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation`.

### Other breaking changes to watch for (not in your current code)

| Change | Fix |
|---|---|
| `Assert.ThrowsException` removed | Use `Assert.ThrowsExactly` |
| `Assert.AreEqual` with format+params | Use string interpolation |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Just use `[ClassCleanup]` |
| `TestContext.Properties.Contains()` | Use `.ContainsKey()` |
| `[Timeout(TestTimeout.Infinite)]` | Use `[Timeout(int.MaxValue)]` |

### Behavioral changes (no build errors, but runtime impact)

